{"title":"Career roadmap · Service Engineer","role":"Service Engineer","summary":"An Automotive Service Engineer diagnoses, maintains, repairs, tests and supports vehicle systems. For an Automobile Engineering graduate, the strongest foundation combines vehicle systems, diagnostics, automotive electronics, engines/EV powertrains, CAN communication, preventive maintenance and customer/service operations.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Service Engineer is a directly aligned career for Automobile Engineering. Depending on the employer, the same pathway may use titles such as Automotive Service Engineer, Technical Service Engineer, Service Advisor, Field Service Engineer or Workshop Engineer."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build vehicle-system knowledge, diagnostics, maintenance, automotive electronics and workshop skills."},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Choose ICE vehicles, EVs, diagnostics, commercial vehicles, automotive electronics or field service."},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Move toward senior diagnostics, technical support, warranty, service operations or regional technical leadership."},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine automotive service expertise with EVs, connected vehicles, ADAS, diagnostics software and predictive maintenance."}],"sections":[{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Engineering mathematics, mechanics, thermodynamics and basic electrical systems"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"tex